# Your Git is configured with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites line endings on
# commit and checkout. That must never happen to binary files, and there is no
# reason to let it churn through the large mesh and input files either.
#
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins, so the general rule comes first
# and the specific overrides come after it.

# Default: let Git normalise line endings for ordinary text files.
*       text=auto

# Large text inputs: keep byte-for-byte as they are.
*.inp   -text
*.obj   -text

# Revit families, the Abaqus CAE database and images: binary, never touch.
*.rfa   binary
*.rvt   binary
*.cae   binary
*.odb   binary
*.png   binary
